81
00:06:41,215 --> 00:06:51,010
I don't remember much of that lecture. The doctor gave me this medicine for my cough, but I don't like it.

82
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:55,455
It seems to make me awfully sleepy and I can't follow my lectures.

83
00:06:55,465 --> 00:07:01,508
Well, if you don't take it, none of us will be able to follow our lectures. All we'll hear is you coughing.

84
00:07:01,518 --> 00:07:02,782
Oh, dear.

85
00:07:02,792 --> 00:07:05,055
Do you think I'll annoy everybody?

86
00:07:05,065 --> 00:07:06,550
Yes.

87
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,330
You could study at home for a couple of days.

88
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:12,277
You know, have some time off until it gets better.

89
00:07:12,287 --> 00:07:16,770
Oh, I couldn't do that. I'd miss too much.

90
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:21,010
And I get really uncomfortable when I have a lot of catching up to do.

91
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:27,290
Last year I missed a whole week when I fell off my bike and had that enormous bandage on my hand.

92
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:30,190
It took me ages to do all the work when I came back.

93
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:34,920
Oh, you worry too much. You can work at home.

94
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:41,710
Just get Mr Grey to tell you which parts of the course book we'll be covering and read it yourself at home.

95
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,230
All he does is go through the book anyway.

96
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,950
You might as well do it yourself.

97
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:51,010
Oh, that's a bit unfair. I think Mr Grey's really nice.

98
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:55,354
He's always willing to stay behind after class if you don't understand something.

99
00:07:55,364 --> 00:08:00,692
Being really nice and never in a hurry doesn't make him a good lecturer.

100
00:08:00,702 --> 00:08:12,065
Anyway, I think you should look after your health first. And ours. If we sit in that small, hot room with you for the next three days, we'll all have your cough by the end of it.

101
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:21,290
Perhaps you're right. I don't care about myself, but I wouldn't like other people to blame me for their illnesses.

102
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:24,970
I have got a bit of a temperature now too.

103
00:08:24,980 --> 00:08:30,690
So maybe I'll go and see Mr Grey after lunch and tell him I won't be at this afternoon's lecture.

104
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:32,726
Or the next two.

105
00:08:32,736 --> 00:08:34,934
Come on, you've got to get better.

106
00:08:34,944 --> 00:08:36,970
I suppose you're right.

107
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:39,990
Then we can all go out as we planned at the weekend.

108
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,430
OK then. I don't want to miss that.

109
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,500
And I do feel ill.

110
