163
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:29,462
I was a small child when I left Vietnam and moved with my family to live in America.

164
00:14:29,472 --> 00:14:34,170
For me and my little brother, it didn't take long before we felt American.

165
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:38,970
But for my parents and two older sisters, it was a different story.

166
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:42,170
The biggest problem for my mother was the language.

167
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:49,510
We were living in New York and although there were quite a lot of Vietnamese families near us, they didn't work in the stores.

168
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:55,850
This meant my mother had to take me with her when she went shopping and I was usually at school.

169
00:14:55,860 --> 00:15:03,510
For my father, the most important thing when we arrived was to find a job. Luckily, he had friends who knew us in Vietnam

170
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:06,098
and they helped him get a job in a factory.

171
00:15:06,108 --> 00:15:11,990
It was hard for him to do that sort of work. In Saigon, he had been a doctor.

172
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,774
My two older sisters went to high school.

173
00:15:14,784 --> 00:15:19,830
They worked hard and did well and the school gave them extra English lessons.

174
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:23,158
Even now though, they speak with Vietnamese accents.

175
00:15:23,168 --> 00:15:29,270
My brother and I are lucky. We may look Vietnamese but we speak with American accents.

176
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,315
My family found the way of life very different.

177
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:39,888
My mother used to spend a lot of time visiting her sisters and brothers and looking after her mother and father.

178
00:15:39,898 --> 00:15:53,250
She feels quite lonely now. She says that in America you live inside your house but in Vietnam, you take your house outside onto the street and share your life with everybody.

179
00:15:53,260 --> 00:16:00,800
I don't remember that but I do find the winters are quite hard to put up with in New York. It's very cold and snows a lot.

180
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:08,652
My father always uses traditional Vietnamese clothes at home and always cooks us rice and noodles.

181
00:16:08,662 --> 00:16:12,970
I must admit, I prefer burgers and chips.

182
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:19,062
Although my friends like to visit us, I often feel a bit embarrassed by my parents' way of life.

183
00:16:19,072 --> 00:16:26,010
They don't understand Americans and I think I am more American than Vietnamese now.

184
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:28,743
I suppose it's sad for them to have such a strange daughter.

